                <pb facs="0490" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg376"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5521: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-14T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                                1924—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 14—1:30
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consul Mukden reports by telegraph heavy troop movements from Mukden southward in
                    last three days. I have no information that they have gone further south than
                    Great Wall.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
